          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.159,
            0.135,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.246,
            0.146,
            0.898,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} area of   \\Delta  OAB  &= \\frac{1}{2}  AB  \\times  OM  = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 21\\sqrt{3} \\times \\frac{21}{2}  cm ^2 \\\\&= \\frac{441}{4} \\sqrt{3}  cm ^2\\end{aligned}\\tag{3}",
          "image_source": "images/page_4_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.243,
            0.899,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, area of the segment $\\mathrm{AYB} = \\left(462 - \\frac{441}{4}\\sqrt{3}\\right) \\mathrm{cm}^2$ [From (1), (2) and (3)] $=   \\frac{21}{4}   ( 88 - 21\\sqrt{3} )  cm ^2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "doc_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.351,
            0.592,
            0.371
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "content": "EXERCISE 11.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.386,
            0.422,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "Unless stated otherwise, use $\\pi = { \\frac { 2 2 } { 7 } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.436,
            0.839,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "**1.** Find the area of a sector of a circle with radius 6 cm if angle of the sector is $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.46,
            0.748,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "**2.** Find the area of a quadrant of a circle whose circumference is 22 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.484,
            0.901,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "**3.** The length of the minute hand of a clock is 14 cm. Find the area swept by the minute hand in 5 minutes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.526,
            0.902,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": "**4.** A chord of a circle of radius 10 cm subtends a right angle at the centre. Find the area of the corresponding : (i) minor segment (ii) major sector. (Use $\\pi   =   3 . 1 4 )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.563,
            0.832,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "**5.** In a circle of radius 21 cm, an arc subtends an angle of $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ at the centre. Find:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.586,
            0.73,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "(i) the length of the arc (ii) area of the sector formed by the arc"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.611,
            0.685,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "(iii) area of the segment formed by the corresponding chord"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.635,
            0.9,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": "**6.** A chord of a circle of radius 15 cm subtends an angle of $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ at the centre. Find the areas of the corresponding minor and major"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.694,
            0.411,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": "(Use   = 3.14 and $\\sqrt{3} = 1.73$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.722,
            0.594,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "**7.** A chord of a circle of radius 12 cm subtends an angle of $1 2 0 \\%$ at the centre. Find the area of the corresponding segment of the circle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.781,
            0.411,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": "(Use   = 3.14 and ${ \\sqrt { 3 } }   =   1 . 7 3 )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.809,
            0.594,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": "**8.** A horse is tied to a peg at one corner of a square shaped grass field of side 15 m by means of a $5$ m long rope (see Fig. 11.8). Find"
